| `get { ... }` takes the answer apart instead of binding it whole, using the
| same field list a handler declares — the two sides of an emit ask the same
| question of the same particle, so they ask it in the same words.
emit Length { value = [1, 2, 3] } to core get { value }
assert value = 3

| `as` renames, for when the answer's word is not the reader's word — and
| here it has to, since `value` is already in scope and nothing may shadow.
emit Length { value = "abcd" } to core get { value as size }
assert size = 4

| A field the answer does not carry is null — exactly what `.field` answers,
| because it is the same read.
emit Length { value = [1] } to core get { value as one, nothing }
assert one = 1
assert nothing = null

| `_class` is an ordinary field, and so is readable like one.
emit Length { value = [] } to core get { _class as kind, value as none }
assert kind = "LengthResult"
assert none = 0

| Nothing holds the answer itself, so a failed emit destructures into nulls
| rather than announcing itself. Ask for it whole when that matters.
emit Length { value = 5 } to core get { value as absent }
assert absent = null
emit Length { value = 5 } to core get whole
assert whole ∈ Exception
